    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 14,
   "tag": "p",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 295,
   "text": "Here are a few ways teams use Loops today:\nDiagnose and dispatch bug reports\nWhen an issue enters triage, a Loop can review its description, comments, and relevant parts of the codebase to recommend a next step. When the path forward is clear, it can start a coding session for an immediate fix.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 3,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 3020,
    "height": 176,
    "widthFraction": 0.43,
    "leftFraction": 0.28,
    "pageFraction": 0.66,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 15,
   "tag": "p",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 244,
   "text": "Generate follow-up work\nWhen a new feature request is created, a Loop can determine whether separate iOS, Android, and web app changes are needed. It can then create the relevant platform-specific issues and route them to the appropriate teams.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 2,
